Subject: [PATCH] The Watchtower app: build it on each tag, for Mac, Windows,
 Linux and Pi

Running Watchtower meant a clone, a venv, fms.init and run.sh, and typing
the vision key into the hub counter. .github/workflows/app.yml builds a
double-click app per OS on each v* tag and attaches it to the release:
first launch runs fms.init into Documents/Watchtower/config, every launch
starts the FMS on :8000 and the YOLOv26-FRC-Model hub counter already
sending to it, and opens a start page with every link and PIN.

The launcher, build spec and smoke test come from YOLOv26-FRC-Model at
the tag in .github/hubcounter-release; this repository's checkout is the
FMS that gets bundled. Each build is smoke-tested (first-launch config,
FMS up, counter preset to it, vision key accepted and a wrong one refused
with 401, Quit stops both) before it is attached.

Checked from YOLOv26-FRC-Model: a packaged linux-x64 build counted a
recorded Einstein match into its own Watchtower live (59.9 fps both hubs),
with /ws updates working. 42 tests pass here.

